
There are two examples here.  The first ("both"; the name refers to having
both puff and recombination sources) employs the familiar treatment of
neutral helium with the only the ground state atom appearing explicitly.
The second ("mboth") has the n=2 metastable species in the problem.
Note that the common reactions involving the ground state are in fact
distinct, having completely different data files.

1. Copy the appropriate main input file into the run directory, e.g.:

cp degas2_both.in ../../SUN/degas2.in

2. Prepare reference data:

cd ../../SUN
gmake datasetup
./datasetup

3. Prepare problem data:

gmake problemsetup
./problemsetup

4. Edit (in src directory) boxgen.web, changing:

@m BOXRUN 0
@m SOLN 1

to
 
@m BOXRUN 42
@m SOLN 0

5. Generate geometry and background files:

cd ../SUN
gmake boxgen
./boxgen

Note that the geometry netCDF file is the same for the two examples,
but the background netCDF files differ.

6. Set the number of flights.  In the background netCDF file for the 
"both" example, set the number of flights to be

source_num_flights = 10000, 10000 ;

And for the "mboth" example:

source_num_flights = 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000 ;

7. Set up the tallies:

gmake tallysetup
./tallysetup

8. Run the code:

gmake flighttest
./flighttest

